==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|psychology|-ical}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsaɪkəˈlɒd͡ʒɪkl̩/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-psychological.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˌsaɪkəˈlɑːd͡ʒɪkl̩/|a=US}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of or pertaining to [[psychology]].
#: {{ux|en|An inkblot test is a method of '''psychological''' evaluation.}}
# Relating to the [[mind]] and [[behavior]] or to the [[mental]], [[emotional]], and behavioral [[characteristic]]s pertaining to a specified [[person]], [[group]], or [[activity]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm concerned about their '''psychological''' well-being.}}
#: {{ux|en|The film was a dark '''psychological''' thriller.}}
# Without an [[objective]], or reasonably logical foundation.
#: {{ux|en|Prices seem to have stopped rising, having hit the '''psychological''' ceiling of just under 100 dollars.}}

